@*
    The one way this UI says "waiting for the server".

    Two variants, chosen by how much is unknown:
      Inline — one region of a rendered page is still resolving; a small spinner and the message sit
               in the flow at text size.
      Block  — the whole panel has nothing to show yet; a skeleton in the rough shape of the content
               holds its place, so the layout does not jump when data arrives and nothing covers the
               page. (The full-panel flight animation was removed on 2026-10-03: it drew attention to
               waiting, cost a large SVG per panel and read as a modal.)
    A non-Bare Inline loader also stands in for a whole panel, so it renders as Block too.

    Always indeterminate: no call this UI makes reports progress (docs/20 §3). Both variants carry
    role="status" with the message, so assistive technology hears the same thing either way.
*@
@if (Variant == LoadingVariant.Block || !Bare)
{
    <div class="@CssClass" role="status" aria-busy="true" aria-live="polite">
        <MudSkeleton SkeletonType="SkeletonType.Text" Width="38%" Height="28px" />
        <MudSkeleton SkeletonType="SkeletonType.Text" Width="92%" />
        <MudSkeleton SkeletonType="SkeletonType.Text" Width="84%" />
        <MudSkeleton SkeletonType="SkeletonType.Rectangle" Height="96px" Class="so-loading-block-body" />
        <span class="so-loading-text">@Message</span>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="@CssClass" role="status" aria-busy="true" aria-live="polite">
        <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="Size.Small" />
        <span class="so-loading-text">@Message</span>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>How much of the surface is pending.</summary>
    public enum LoadingVariant
    {
        /// <summary>A region inside an otherwise rendered page.</summary>
        Inline,

        /// <summary>The whole panel, with nothing else to show yet.</summary>
        Block
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// What is being waited for, in the operator's terms ("Yetkileriniz doğrulanıyor…"), not the
    /// mechanism. This is announced to assistive technology, so it must stand alone.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Message { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Layout to use. Defaults to the in-flow form.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public LoadingVariant Variant { get; set; } = LoadingVariant.Inline;

    /// <summary>
    /// Set when the element already sits inside a panel, to avoid drawing a second border around it.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Bare { get; set; }

    // A loader that stands in for a whole panel becomes a skeleton; one inside a panel stays inline.
    private string CssClass => Variant == LoadingVariant.Block || !Bare ? "so-loading so-loading--block" : "so-loading";
}
